cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Tourism service supply chains in ten emerging economies:
  data collection and analysis notebooks
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying materials, please
  cite both the archived release and the associated article.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Douglas
    family-names: De Souza Rodrigues
    email: rodriguesdouglas@id.uff.br
    affiliation: >-
      Production Engineering Department, Fluminense Federal
      University, Petropolis, RJ, Brazil
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7473-7425'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/douglaskorvo/tourism_supply_chain'
abstract: >-
  Notebooks documenting the retrieval of a corpus of user-generated
  tourism reviews from the Google Places API and its analysis, for a
  study of tourism service supply chains in ten emerging economies.
  The raw corpus is not redistributed because platform terms of
  service restrict redistribution of Places content.
keywords:
  - tourism service supply chain
  - service disruption
  - user-generated content
  - dictionary-based content analysis
  - reproducibility
  - emerging economies
license: MIT
